<title>CHINA: HK's Goldlion year net up 6.15 percent.</title>
<headline>HK's Goldlion year net up 6.15 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   35.7     vs  37.9 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    12.0     vs  12.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil	vs  3.06 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    300.68   vs  283.25</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,179.88 vs  1,229.04</p>
<p>    Company name		 Goldlion Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  August 5-8</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   August 28</p>
<p>NOTE - Goldlion Holdings is a men's clothing manufacturer.</p>
<p>Share earnings are based on the weighted average of 841.3 million shares vs 746.8 million.</p>
<p>Total dividend for the year is 18 H.K. cents (including an interim dividend of six cents) vs same.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
